{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And the kings who were with him.</b> Those who were with him in the campaign of <b>the Valley of Siddim</b>, and among them <b>Amraphel</b>." "<b>And they struck the Rephaim and the Zuzim and the Emim.</b> All of these were subjects of the five kings and fought on their behalf. By this Scripture indicates that the five kings were great, and it indicates the might of the four kings who defeated them. From this the greatness of Abraham's valor is known, and the stratagems of his warfare, and his devotion to his kinsman — that he delivered himself to prevail over them and to rescue his nephew and his property from the sword of their mouth, and among their pursuers he cast prey beyond what he sought, through HaShem's compassion upon him."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:04.737002811Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}